From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] update: share reboot protection across activations and programmers

Keep one shared flock reference per activation and programmer. Only a final
release may remove the global reboot guard. This also protects BIOS shells
that outlive a software updater restart. Reconcile serialized drop-ins with
systemd immediately, and make repeated guard enable operations idempotent.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD update policy]

diff --git a/bmc/activation.hpp b/bmc/activation.hpp
--- a/bmc/activation.hpp
+++ b/bmc/activation.hpp
@@ -131,18 +131,9 @@
      *  @param[in] bus    - The Dbus bus object
      *  @param[in] path   - The Dbus object path
      */
-    ActivationBlocksTransition(sdbusplus::bus_t& bus, const std::string& path) :
-        ActivationBlocksTransitionInherit(bus, path.c_str(),
-                                          action::emit_interface_added),
-        bus(bus)
-    {
-        enableRebootGuard();
-    }
-
-    ~ActivationBlocksTransition() override
-    {
-        disableRebootGuard();
-    }
+    ActivationBlocksTransition(sdbusplus::bus_t& bus, const std::string& path);
+
+    ~ActivationBlocksTransition() override;
 
     ActivationBlocksTransition(const ActivationBlocksTransition&) = delete;
     ActivationBlocksTransition& operator=(const ActivationBlocksTransition&) =
@@ -153,6 +144,7 @@
 
   private:
     sdbusplus::bus_t& bus;
+    int rebootGuardFd = -1;
 
